			"notes": "Due to problems involving versioning, instead of continuing from 0.1.0, we're proceeding from 2.0.0 starting this update. Whoops.\n\n# Physics Changes\n* Replaced the pretty primitive built-in proprietary physics engine with Nvidia PhysX. This allows for more stable physics\n  * Future updates might allow for the ability to change physics engine from the config. Planned physics engines to include are Jolt and Krunch.\n  * PLEASE DO NOT ASSUME THAT THIS WILL MAKE IT ONLY WORK ON NVIDIA GPUS. Physics operations still run on the CPU, so if you have say an AMD GPU nothing will change.\n* SHIPS CAN NOW COLLIDE WITH EACH OTHER\n* Ships on the ground no longer spasm and spin by small increments \n* Replaced numerical based masses with enums that provide fixed masses. This means the config section for block masses must now use those enums\n  * The following are the enums with their associated mass in kg:\n    * NONE (0 kg)\n    * VERY_LIGHT (500 kg)\n    * LIGHT (1000 kg)\n    * HEAVY (8000 kg)\n    * VERY_HEAVY (20000 kg)\n* Gyroscope Stabilizer now works properly, and no longer causes ships its attached to to spasm or spin randomly. It now stabilizes as expected\n* Placing a Captain's Chair on the ship now causes ship to be truly aligned no matter what\n\n# Other Changes, Additions, and Fixes\n* Rewrote VS World to no longer use Kotlin. The project is now 100% java. This means no more need to install Forgelin Continuous!\n* Added the Buoyancy Tank, which applies buoyancy so that your ship can now float in water! The force it applies can be configured in the config for VS Control. Recipe can be checked with JEI.\n* Lots of reforms to how wires work\n  * Wires are no longer durability based. Instead, connecting two nodes now just consumes a wire\n  * Shears can be used to remove wires, just right click a node with a shear to remove that node's connections (the used wires will drop as items too)\n  * Breaking a node makes the used wires drop as items too\n  * While connecting two nodes, a message will show up on the hotbar telling you that you are creating a connection.\n* Network relays now automatically break when their supporting block breaks\n* Piloting now gets cancelled when Ship Helm, Captain's Chair, or Boat Chair is broken\n* When building a ship in water, nearby water sources now update properly\n* Blocks mined with tool that makes them break quickly (say an efficiency tool) no longer get rolled back\n* Fixed a walk through walls hack\n* Added configurable option to negate fall damage when falling onto a ship\n* Added configurable list of entities that ships cannot collide with (they will phase thru the ship)\n* Fixed mysterious shadow appearing in where ship was constructed upon reloading the world\n* Fixed tile entities and entities being invisible unless nearby when riding captains chair or boat chair\n* Added configurable list of chair entities to ensure that when a player sits on a chair or other sittable block from other mods, they are positioned properly even when the ship moves, and will not be kicked off violently when unmounting. By default (and tested) this includes:\n  * All sittable blocks from [Mr Crayfish's furniture mod rebuilt](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/mrcrayfish-furniture-mod-rebuilt)\n  * Chairs from [Rustic](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/rustic)\n  * Chairs and slabs from [Sit](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/sit)\n  * Seats from [Bibliocraft Reshelved](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/bibliocraft-reshelved)\n* Entities spawned with spawn eggs on a ship are no longer attached to the ship\n* Physics Infuser UI buttons no longer override the JEI menu\n* Dummy blocks are now hidden from JEI menu\n* Fixed crash when loading a world with [chance cubes](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/chance-cubes) installed\n* Added texture for water pump\n* Water pump now has an adjustable range, which can be changed by right clicking on it. It can be changed between 3 x 3, 5 x 5, and 7 x 7.\n\n..."
		},
